{
 "annotations": {
  "destructiveHint": false,
  "idempotentHint": true,
  "openWorldHint": true,
  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "skypeek: satellite passes over a location (ISS and others)"
 },
 "description": "skypeek: Predict satellite passes over a location. For sun and moon times use sun_moon_times. Returns the passes of a satellite (default the ISS) over a point in the next 1-3 days: start, highest and end times with azimuth and elevation, duration, and whether the pass is visible to the eye. SGP4 predictions, not observations, from CelesTrak orbital elements (only derived pass times are returned; no endorsement by CelesTrak implied). Satellites: CelesTrak's 'stations' and 'visual' groups plus NOAA 15 / 18 / 19; another NORAD id is a 422 (not charged). At most 40 passes. A cold orbital-data cache or an upstream outage can be a 503 (not charged; retry). Typically under 1 s; with a cold orbital-data cache up to a minute or more (a 503 when too slow, not charged: retry). Price: USD 0.002. Free: 5 skypeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/iss-pass-times-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
